{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The basic preact app example to get started with the TanStack preact-store."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { render } from \"preact\";\nimport { createStore, useSelector } from \"@tanstack/preact-store\";\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Preact components too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\n// This will only re-render when `state[animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render\n\nconst Display = ({ animal }) => {\n  const count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[animal]);\n  return <div>{`${animal}: ${count}`}</div>;\n};\n\nconst updateState = (animal) => {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n};\nconst Increment = ({ animal }) => (\n  <button onClick={() => updateState(animal)}>My Friend Likes {animal}</button>\n);\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n      <p>\n        Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends\n        like cats or dogs\n      </p>\n      <Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n      <Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n      <Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n      <Display animal=\"cats\" />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nrender(<App />, document.getElementById(\"root\"));","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore"},{"type":"text","value":" remains available as a deprecated alias to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe basic preact app example to get started with the TanStack preact-store.\n\n```tsx\nimport { render } from \"preact\";\nimport { createStore, useSelector } from \"@tanstack/preact-store\";\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Preact components too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\n// This will only re-render when `state[animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render\n\nconst Display = ({ animal }) => {\n  const count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[animal]);\n  return <div>{`${animal}: ${count}`}</div>;\n};\n\nconst updateState = (animal) => {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n};\nconst Increment = ({ animal }) => (\n  <button onClick={() => updateState(animal)}>My Friend Likes {animal}</button>\n);\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n      <p>\n        Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends\n        like cats or dogs\n      </p>\n      <Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n      <Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n      <Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n      <Display animal=\"cats\" />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nrender(<App />, document.getElementById(\"root\"));\n```\n\n`useStore` remains available as a deprecated alias to `useSelector`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\nid: quick-start\n---\n\nThe basic preact app example to get started with the TanStack preact-store.\n\n```tsx\nimport { render } from \"preact\";\nimport { createStore, useSelector } from \"@tanstack/preact-store\";\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Preact components too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\n// This will only re-render when `state[animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render\n\nconst Display = ({ animal }) => {\n  const count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[animal]);\n  return <div>{`${animal}: ${count}`}</div>;\n};\n\nconst updateState = (animal) => {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n};\nconst Increment = ({ animal }) => (\n  <button onClick={() => updateState(animal)}>My Friend Likes {animal}</button>\n);\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n      <p>\n        Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends\n        like cats or dogs\n      </p>\n      <Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n      <Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n      <Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n      <Display animal=\"cats\" />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nrender(<App />, document.getElementById(\"root\"));\n```\n\n`useStore` remains available as a deprecated alias to `useSelector`.\n"}
